// i hate febuilder
#define TRUE 1
#define FALSE 0

// ASMC 
#define EnactAutoRepair "ASMC RefreshItemsASMC|1"
#define EnactAutoRepair(uses) "SVAL s1 uses; ASMC RefreshItemsASMC|1"

// convoy size, change if expanding convoy
#define MaxConvoy 128

// if true, weapons at 0 durability will have reduced stats and still be equippable.
#define EQUIP_BROKEN_WEAPONS TRUE

// if false, magic weapons will be exempt from the above rule
#define EQUIP_BROKEN_MAGIC FALSE

// broken weapon table macro
//#define BrokenWeaponEntry(name, desc, mt, hit, wt, crit, rng) "SHORT name desc mt hit wt crit rng"
#define BrokenWeaponEntry(mt,hit,wt,crit) "BYTE mt hit wt crit"

// filler numbers, change to your specifications
//The default macro order is wrong. Name/desc are known issues, but "hit" is weight.
//And the alleged lance entry didn't change the broken lance. The sword entry did.
//It has 50 might and 60 weight, while hit and crit are both zero.
//How did that happen? Testing the rapier now.
//That has utterly nonsensical stats. 16 might, one hit, one crit, 17 weight?
//I wonder if the issue is the name/description still being part of the macro,
//but since they're not being changed anymore, it throws the rest off?
//Now that I look at the bytes a bit closer, yeah that's exactly what's
//happening. 0x10 0x01 0x11 0x01 matches the reported numbers.
//In fact, the non-Skillsys version has a shortened macro. Ah, copy-paste errors.
ALIGN 4
BrokenWeaponTable:
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,20,20,0) //Broken Sword
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,20,20,0) //Broken Lance
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,20,20,0) //Broken Axe
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,20,20,0) //Broken Bow
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,0,0,0) //Broken Staff, shouldn't matter
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,0,0,0) //Empty Book (anima)
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,0,0,0) //Empty Book (light)
BrokenWeaponEntry(0,0,0,0) //Empty Book (dark)

